---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { liveStates, type LiveState } from '../../data/states';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return liveStates.map((state) => ({
    params: { state: state.slug },
    props: { state },
  }));
}

const { state } = Astro.props as { state: LiveState };

const pageUrl = new URL(`/growing-zones/${state.slug}/`, Astro.site).href;
const title = `${state.name} Growing Zones & Frost Dates (USDA 2023 Map)`;
const description = `What USDA hardiness zone is ${state.name} in? Zone ${state.zoneRangeLow} to ${state.zoneRangeHigh} across the state, major city zones, frost dates, and what actually grows well.`;

const formattedLastUpdated = new Date(state.lastUpdated + 'T00:00:00').toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
});

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', Astro.site).href },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Growing Zones', item: new URL('/growing-zones/', Astro.site).href },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: state.name, item: pageUrl },
  ],
};

const articleJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: `What Growing Zone Is ${state.name} In?`,
  description,
  url: pageUrl,
  datePublished: '2026-09-06',
  dateModified: state.lastUpdated,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'HarvestMath Editors', url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'HarvestMath', url: Astro.site!.href },
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': pageUrl },
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} rawTitle canonical={pageUrl}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbJsonLd)} slot="head" />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleJsonLd)} slot="head" />

  <section class="border-b border-moss-100 bg-moss-50/60">
    <div class="container-wide py-12 sm:py-16">
      <nav class="flex flex-wrap text-sm text-bark-500" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-moss-800">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <a href="/growing-zones/" class="hover:text-moss-800">Growing Zones</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span class="text-bark-700">{state.name}</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-bark-900 sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">
        What Growing Zone Is {state.name} In?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-bark-500">
        Last updated <time datetime={state.lastUpdated}>{formattedLastUpdated}</time>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-wide py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose prose-bark max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-bark-900 prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:scroll-mt-24 prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:font-semibold prose-a:text-moss-700 prose-strong:text-bark-900">

        <p>
          {state.zoneRangeLow === state.zoneRangeHigh ? (
            <>{state.name} falls entirely within USDA hardiness zone <strong>{state.zoneRangeLow}</strong>, according to the 2023 USDA Plant Hardiness Zone Map &mdash; one of the more spatially uniform areas on the map.</>
          ) : (
            <>{state.name} spans USDA hardiness zone <strong>{state.zoneRangeLow} to {state.zoneRangeHigh}</strong> across its major population centers, according to the 2023 USDA Plant Hardiness Zone Map. That's a real range, not a single number &mdash; where you fall in it depends on where in the state you actually are.</>
          )}
        </p>

        <h2 id={`${state.slug}-usda-hardiness-zones`}>{state.name}'s USDA Hardiness Zones</h2>
        <p>
          Here's how the zone shifts across {state.name}'s major cities:
        </p>
        <div class="not-prose my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-moss-100">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-moss-50">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-bark-900">City</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-bark-900">USDA Zone</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-moss-100">
              {state.cities.map((c) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">{c.city}</td>
                  <td class="p-3">{c.zone}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          For your exact zone by ZIP code, use the <a href="/calculators/hardiness-zone-finder/">Hardiness Zone Finder</a> &mdash; and for what a zone number actually measures (and doesn't), see <a href="/blog/usda-hardiness-zones-explained/">how zones actually work</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id={`frost-dates-in-${state.slug}`}>Frost Dates in {state.name}</h2>
        {state.coldestBand.zone === state.warmestBand.zone ? (
          <>
            <p>
              Because {state.name} sits in a single zone, frost dates are consistent statewide:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Zone {state.coldestBand.zone}</strong>: average last frost {state.coldestBand.lastFrostRange}, average first frost {state.coldestBand.firstFrostRange}.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p>
              Frost dates track zone, so they shift across {state.name} the same way the zone number does:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>{state.coldestBand.label}</strong> (zone {state.coldestBand.zone}): average last frost {state.coldestBand.lastFrostRange}, average first frost {state.coldestBand.firstFrostRange}.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>{state.warmestBand.label}</strong> (zone {state.warmestBand.zone}): average last frost {state.warmestBand.lastFrostRange}, average first frost {state.warmestBand.firstFrostRange}.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </>
        )}
        <p>
          These are averages, not guarantees &mdash; for your specific frost window, use the <a href="/calculators/frost-date-calculator/">Frost Date Calculator</a>. For a full vegetable-by-vegetable planting calendar already calculated from {state.name}'s frost dates, see the <a href={`/planting-calendar/${state.slug}/`}>{state.name} Planting Calendar</a>.
        </p>

        {state.climateNote && (
          <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-2xl border border-moss-200 bg-moss-50/60 p-5">
            <p class="text-sm text-bark-700">{state.climateNote}</p>
          </div>
        )}

        <h2 id={`what-grows-well-in-${state.slug}`}>What Grows Well in {state.name}'s Zones</h2>
        <p>
          A few real, zone-appropriate picks recommended by {state.plantsSourceLabel} for {state.name} landscapes &mdash; not an exhaustive list, but a genuine starting point:
        </p>
        <ul>
          {state.plants.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{p.commonName}</strong>{p.scientificName && <> ({p.scientificName})</>}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <div class="not-prose my-8 rounded-2xl border border-moss-200 bg-moss-50/60 p-6">
          <p class="text-bark-700">
            Ready to find your exact zone? Use the <a href="/calculators/hardiness-zone-finder/" class="font-medium underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-moss-900">Hardiness Zone Finder</a> &mdash; enter your ZIP code for a precise match against the 2023 USDA map.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="sources-and-further-reading">Sources &amp; further reading</h2>
        <p>
          Zone and city data checked against the official <a href="https://planthardiness.ars.usda.gov/" rel="noopener">USDA Plant Hardiness Zone Map</a>. Plant recommendations sourced from <a href={state.plantsSourceUrl} rel="noopener">{state.plantsSourceLabel}</a>.
          {state.climateNoteSourceUrl && state.climateNoteSourceLabel && (
            <> Climate note sourced from <a href={state.climateNoteSourceUrl} rel="noopener">{state.climateNoteSourceLabel}</a>.</>
          )}
          {' '}For more on how we build and verify reference data across this site, see our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
